    "https://www.queens.edu/careers/": {
      "title": "Why Work",
      "description": "Why Work at Queens? - Queens University of Charlotte Skip to Main Content Apply Visit Give Request Info Search Queens University logo Search This is Queens Mission, Vision & Values History Leadership Diversity & Inclusion Sustainability Alumni Careers @ Queens Campus Directory Student Experience Student Life Living on Campus Charlotte Student Resources Veterans Academics Academic Affairs Majors & Programs Graduate & Professional General Education Schools & Colleges Internships & Careers Study Abroad Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Tuition, Scholarships & Aid Athletics Community Arts at Queens Learning Society Friends of the Library Host an Event University Programs Affiliated Centers Close Search Top Searched null Helpful Links Apply Visit Give Request Info Why Work at Queens? Home Why Work at Queens? Why Work at Queens? Career Opportunities at Queens Graduate Assistant Opportunities at Queens Queens University of Charlotte provides a workplace culture where every employee is valued and provided with opportunities to grow professionally, knowing they are respected for their unique gifts. Core Values Life at Queens is guided by our motto, “Not to be served, but to serve.” We are committed to serving the greater Charlotte community by providing time and opportunities for employees to give back. Employee Resource Groups We offer a variety of ERGs, open to all, which foster community amongst our faculty and staff. Benefits & Work-Life Balance We promote a culture of health and wellness by offering a robust package of medical and work-life balance benefits, including flexible work, fitness facilities, tuition remission, and generous paid time-off options. Faculty Specific Support Hayworth Center for Digital Learning The Hayworth Center for Digital Learning supports our Queens faculty by offering a concierge suite of support services throughout the entire learning experience – from design, to development, to delivery of instruction. We support our faculty in the creation of high-quality, student-centered digital learning experiences founded on principles of pedagogy, andragogy and curricular design. The Hayworth Center offers faculty one-on-one consultations and training to take advantage of digital tools in the classroom, whether seated or online. Our approachable team is committed to ensuring faculty have access to resources and learning opportunities to grow in their own teaching practices. Center for the Advancement of Faculty Excellence (CAFÉ) Directly aligned the Queens strategic framework, CAFÉ aims to deliver the highest quality support for Queens faculty at all career stages through onboarding and orientation, in-person and online resources, collegial learning experiences, competitive funding, innovative learning spaces and technology, consulting, and collaborative problem-solving. The CAFÉ designs, develops, facilitates, and delivers personalized support through one-on-one consultations and practical 24/7 online resources, multi-day institutes and workshops, faculty work groups and more. Explore Careers at Queens Contact Us 1900 Selwyn Ave. Charlotte, NC 28274 704-337-2200 Info For Family & Friends School Counselors News Media Policies Accreditation Non-discrimination Policy Policy & Procedures Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Twitter TikTok © 2026 Queens University of Charlotte"
    },
    "https://www.queens.edu/internships/": {
      "title": "Vandiver Center for Career Development",
      "description": "Vandiver Center for Career Development - Queens University of Charlotte Skip to Main Content Apply Visit Give Request Info Search Queens University logo Search This is Queens Mission, Vision & Values History Leadership Diversity & Inclusion Sustainability Alumni Careers @ Queens Campus Directory Student Experience Student Life Living on Campus Charlotte Student Resources Veterans Academics Academic Affairs Majors & Programs Graduate & Professional General Education Schools & Colleges Internships & Careers Study Abroad Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Tuition, Scholarships & Aid Athletics Community Arts at Queens Learning Society Friends of the Library Host an Event University Programs Affiliated Centers Close Search Top Searched null Helpful Links Apply Visit Give Request Info Vandiver Center for Career Development Home Vandiver Center for Career Development Vandiver Center for Career Development Meet the Team Career Development Guide First Destination Report Handshake Online Job Board Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Alumni Parents & Families Employers Employer Expectations & Policies Hiring International Students The Vandiver Center for Career Development (VCCD) supports Queens students in everything from career exploration, internships, and jobs to graduate school planning. We use a holistic approach to prepare students for their future. Internships Did you know that 100% of Queens undergraduates complete an internship? That’s right! Internships allow you to apply what you’ve learned in the classroom in a real-life setting. These are what an internship can do for you: Help you determine your interests Learn new skills Make connections with industry professionals Learn more about the industry Develop an impressive resume Practice real world application of skills Career Development By developing relationships with employers, we develop programs and courses aligned with what employers want. Our career coaches are experts in the top industries and provide specialized career services. As a result, students are able to see how their skills, desires, and goals line up with the latest industry trends. The following are some of the programs and curricula we offer: Employer taught professional development curriculum. Students are taught by university relations recruiters and learning/development professionals representing Novant Health, Duke Energy, etc. Industry-specific networking events. Employer mock interviews. Employer collaborations on career prep workshops. Industry-specific coaching. We serve not only undergrads and graduate students but also Queens alumni. In fact, alums receive services for life at no cost. Top Organizations Employing Queens Graduates Accenture, Ally, American Red Cross, Atrium Health, Bank of America, Beasley Media, Charlotte Observer, Carolina Panthers, Charlotte Hornets, City of Charlotte, Continental Tires, Duke Energy, Ernst & Young, ESPN, Fox Sports, Google, Goldman Sachs, KPMG, Lowe’s Companies, Maersk, NASCAR, NBC, Novant, PwC, TIAA, UBS, Wells Fargo, YMCA Top Schools Recruiting Our Graduates Baylor University, Boston College, Carnegie Mellon University, Columbia University, Cornell University, Duke University, Georgetown University, Johns Hopkins Medical School, London School of Economics, Medical University of South Carolina, New York University, Princeton University, Rice University, University of Cambridge, University of Chicago, University of Michigan, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, University of Virginia, Vanderbilt University, Wake Forest University Traditional Undergraduate Student Data (Based on Class of 2024) See our First Destination Report for all the information! Graduate Student Data (Based on Class of 2024) 96% of our graduate students agree that their master’s degree significantly helped them achieve their planned career changes or advancement goals. 93% of our graduate students agree that completing a master’s degree at Queens increased their workplace confidence. Companies represented in Class of 2024 A & E Networks, Aetna, Ally, Atrium Health, AvidXchange, Bank of America, Beasley Media Group, Blumenthal Performing Arts, Charlotte Mecklenburg School System, Charlotte Pipe and Foundry, Citibank, Collins Aerospace, Continental Tires, Cushman & Wakefield, Duke Energy, Duke University Health System, EY, Jeld-Wen, Lowe’s Companies, Maersk, Mecklenburg County, Novant Health, NYU Langone Hospital, OrthoCarolina, Pfizer, Red Ventures, U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, Vanguard, Wells Fargo, Wray Ward Upcoming Events Check out our events designed to help you advance your career, from expert panels to networking events and everything in between. Follow Us Instagram Contact Us 1900 Selwyn Ave. Charlotte, NC 28274 704-337-2200 Info For Family & Friends School Counselors News Media Policies Accreditation Non-discrimination Policy Policy & Procedures Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Twitter TikTok © 2026 Queens University of Charlotte"
    },
    "https://www.queens.edu/careers/why-work-at-queens/career-opportunities-at-queens/": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Career Opportunities at Queens - Queens University of Charlotte Skip to Main Content Apply Visit Give Request Info Search Queens University logo Search This is Queens Mission, Vision & Values History Leadership Diversity & Inclusion Sustainability Alumni Careers @ Queens Campus Directory Student Experience Student Life Living on Campus Charlotte Student Resources Veterans Academics Academic Affairs Majors & Programs Graduate & Professional General Education Schools & Colleges Internships & Careers Study Abroad Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Tuition, Scholarships & Aid Athletics Community Arts at Queens Learning Society Friends of the Library Host an Event University Programs Affiliated Centers Close Search Top Searched null Helpful Links Apply Visit Give Request Info Career Opportunities at Queens Home Why Work at Queens? Why Work at Queens? Why Work at Queens? Career Opportunities at Queens Graduate Assistant Opportunities at Queens The mission of Queens University of Charlotte is to be a convener, promoting open dialogue, fostering intellectual growth, and providing new perspectives and cultural experiences for the campus community and beyond. To this end, the university recruits talented faculty, staff, and students from across the United States and around the world. Queens encourages applications from women, people of color, people with disabilities, and members of other protected classes and historically minoritized communities. The university also invites applications from individuals who are prepared to provide a rich and varied educational experience to our increasingly diverse student body and to collaborate with colleagues to make Queens an equitable and inclusive place to live, learn, and work. We invite you to learn more about the university’s mission, vision, and values . A candidate will only be contacted if their qualifications match the job requirements. We respectfully request you not to call or email regarding the status of your submission. Job Postings Athletic Postings Manager – Athletic Trainer Equal Opportunity Employer Queens University of Charlotte is an equal-opportunity employer and is firmly committed to supporting and celebrating all forms of diversity. Queens does not discriminate based on race, color, gender, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and conditions related to pregnancy or childbirth), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, age, national origin, disability, political beliefs, veteran status, genetic information or any characteristic protected by law in the administration of its educational and admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic programs, employment and hiring policies, or other university-administered programs. Any applicant for employment who needs any reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the Director of Human Resources ( hr@queens.edu , 704-337-2297). Required Documentation & Background Check In compliance with the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986, employment is contingent upon new employees providing documents verifying U.S. citizenship or documents verifying legal permission to work in the United States. After an offer has been extended and accepted, Queens conducts confidential background investigations on new employees as part of the hiring process. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of the background check. New employees must be fully vaccinated when they first report to work at Queens. E-Verify Information Federal law requires all employers to verify that newly hired individuals are authorized to work in the United States and to complete an Employment Verification (Form I-9) for each new employee. Newly hired employees are required to provide original documents that confirm legally acceptable proof of their identity and authorization to work in the US within 3 business days of their first day. E-Verify is an internet-based system operated by the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) in partnership with the Social Security Administration (SSA) that allows participating employers to electronically verify the employment eligibility of new hires and the validity of their Social Security Numbers. Through participation in the E-Verify program, we electronically verify the employment eligibility and Social Security Number validity of all new hires. Review the documents below for more information. E-Verify Information: Spanish Right to Work Information: English | Spanish Annual Security Report The Queens University of Charlotte Annual Security Report , in conjunction with the Department of Education’s Jeanne Clery Act, discloses our campus crime statistics and details our security policies. Queens will provide a paper copy of this report upon request. Contact Us 1900 Selwyn Ave. Charlotte, NC 28274 704-337-2200 Info For Family & Friends School Counselors News Media Policies Accreditation Non-discrimination Policy Policy & Procedures Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Twitter TikTok © 2026 Queens University of Charlotte"
    },
